WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.534
Your party announced

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.102
that the

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.236
first Republican debate

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.838
will be in August in Milwaukee,

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:05.905
Wisconsin.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.440
Will candidates

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.809
be required to sign a pledge

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.144
saying that they will support

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.812
whomever becomes the nominee

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.647
in order to get on that debate stage?

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.082
We haven't put the criteria out,

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.851
but I expect a pledge will be part of it.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.619
It was part of 2016

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.388
I think it's kind of a no brainer, right?

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.789
If you're going to be on the Republican

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.657
National Committee debate stage

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.126
asking voters to support you,

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.060
you should say I'm going

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.028
to support the voters

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:28.862
and who they choose

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.131
as the nominee as RNC chair.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.999
If I said I wouldn't support

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.401
the Republican nominee,

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.269
I would be removed from office.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:36.669
I would

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.637
I be rightly removed

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:38.805
to be part of our bylaws

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.041
and I would be kicked out as RNC chair.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.575
Anybody getting on the Republican

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.344
National Committee debate stage

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.478
should be able to say

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.946
I will support the will of the voters

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.648
and the eventual nominee of our party.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.183
I want you to listen to what former

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.951
President Donald Trump said

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.019
a couple of weeks ago

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:53.753
in an interview

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.256
with conservative radio host Hugh

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.557
Hewitt on this very topic.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:00:59.793
If you're

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.226
not the

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.428
nominee, will you support

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.696
whoever the GOP nominee is?

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.531
It would depend.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.432
I would

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.466
give you the same answer

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.835
I gave in 2016 during the debate.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.370
It would have to depend on

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.338
who the nominee was.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.641
So are you prepared to block the former

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.643
presidential candidate in 2016?

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.177
I did.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.812
Everybody signed it in 2016.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.113
But this is about the here and the now.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.014
He didn't commit to it.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.248
I think they're all going to sign it.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.049
I really do.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.117
I think the voters

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.885
are very intent on winning

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.253
and they do not want to see

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.488
a debate stage of people

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.956
saying I'm not going to support this guy.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.291
I'm not going to support this guy.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.192
What they need to say

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.860
is I'm going to do everything I can

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.195
to defeat Joe Biden.

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.629
And that means supporting

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.131
the nominee of the Republican Party.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.232
You can't see a scenario

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:39.999
where Donald Trump

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.301
would just skip the debate

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:42.969
if he's forced to sign something saying,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.071
I want to be on the debate stage.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.439
I think President Trump

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.241
would like to be on the debate stage.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.309
That's what he likes to do.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.444
And I expect they'll all be there.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.312
I want to look at it

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.746
sort of from the other side of this,

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.048
which is that others

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.383
who are not Donald Trump candidates

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.952
like potential candidates

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.019
like former Governor

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:00.920
Asa Hutchinson,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.590
they're not happy about this requirement.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.158
He said, quote, For leaders

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.392
such as myself who believe

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:06.960
Donald Trump

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.628
is not the right direction

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.662
for the country.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.698
And I said specifically, the January six

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.233
disqualified him.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.100
What would

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.002
that would certainly make it a problem

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.670
for me to give in across the board

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.305
inclusive pledge.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.440
How do you make candidates

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.208
like I like him,

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:25.411
given the reality of what has happened on

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.915
January six, go against his.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.884
What he's saying is his principle.

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.452
I think you support the voters.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.720
The voters get to choose.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.822
And if the Republican voters

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.656
pick the nominee,

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.191
then everybody on that debate stage

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:38.725
who is running

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:39.492
and the Republican

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.527
National Committee debate

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.861
in the Republican National Committee

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.829
primaries should say, I'm

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.763
going to support the nominee.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.598
Listen, I say this all the time, Dana.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.033
I am Mitt Romney's niece

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.468
and I was appointed to the RNC

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:49.469
by Donald Trump.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:50.970
And I would support both support

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.437
both of them

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.172
if they were the nominee

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.374
of our party over Joe Biden.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:55.208
But I don't know if they would

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.142
support each other.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.111
We have to come together as a party.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.812
We saw big races

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:00.280
lost in a

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.848
cycle because of Republicans

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:04.017
refusing to support other Republicans.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.852
And unless we fix this in our party,

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.520
unless we start coming together,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.155
we will not win in 20, 24.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:11.457
And I am committed to making sure

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.659
we come together as a party.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.094
Understandable.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:18.031
But at the same time, what you hear

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.300
somebody like Asa Hutchinson, who is he

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.201
is no moderate.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.802
He is a tried and true

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.270
conservative Republican.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.772
Effectively saying is

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:28.341
you would be asking him to put country

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.076
to a party over country.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.544
You'd be asking him to put party over.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.812
Oh, I don't see it that way.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.846
That may be how he sees it.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:34.948
I don't see it that way.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.783
I think if the voters choose

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.551
Donald Trump to be the nominee,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.719
if they choose Mike Pence,

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.153
if they choose

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.021
Mike Pompeo or Asa Hutchinson,

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.489
everybody should support the

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.490
will of the voters

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.326
and we're not going to defeat Joe Biden

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:47.961
if we get in this tit for tat of

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.462
I'm not going to support this nominee

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:50.630
and I'm not going to support this one.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.064
So that's why

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.399
we want to put this to bed early.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.300
This is a pledge

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.401
that's been in existence.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.970
It was there in 2016.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.870
And we should make sure

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.972
that every candidate

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.640
on the Republican National Committee

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.775
debate stage does what I have to do,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.577
which is support the nominee of our party

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.080
One more question on this.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.048
How do you enforce it?

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:09.882
Once, once,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.451
once you get

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:14.454
to the point where there is a

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:15.488
presumptive nominee,

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.522
the debates are going to be over.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.291
So how do you even enforce this?

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:18.858
We're saying

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:19.192
you're not going

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.093
to get on the debate stage

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.961
unless you make this pledge.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.496
And I think people in our party

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:24.464
really want to see that.

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.865
They want to see us come together.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.433
They don't want the infighting.

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:28.568
And by the way,

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.869
it's not a good look, right?

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.237
If we're fighting each other.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.171
What young person

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.239
I think of my 17 year

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.540
old in my 19 year old,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.208
they don't want to see

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.409
a Republican Party fighting.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.543
They want to see us talk about

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:37.977
how we're going

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:38.911
to make their lives better.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.979
They're going to come out of college

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:40.513
with a job.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.648
We're going to tackle the border.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:42.982
We're going to tackle that now.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.384
They don't want to see us infighting.

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:45.752
Let's talk about issues.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.086
That's what we need to get back to.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:47.387
And that's

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.788
how we're going to win in 20, 24.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.023
Any other

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.658
requirements that you believe

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:52.792
should be there

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.494
when it comes to a threshold?

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:55.895
Oh, I think there should be a threshold,

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:56.863
and that makes sense.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.464
We'll get that out probably closer.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.866
Do you think the debate three,

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:00.533
we're not going

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.602
ahead of our debate committee

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.770
We've been talking about this

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.537
for a year and a half,

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.638
but there should be some threshold

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.707
the Democrats have that in 2016.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:08.708
You want to make sure that

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.076
people are on the debate stage

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.177
who are running for president.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:11.878
We don't want people

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:12.912
running for book deals

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.781
or a media contracts

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:16.149
or cabinet positions.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.283
We want people there

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:17.750
who are running

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.385
for president of the United States.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.286
Can you promise.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.088
We we're talking about promises now.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:25.058
That whomever the Republican nominee is

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:26.793
ultimately

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:29.729
will accept the results in 20, 24.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:30.663
I expect that

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.465
they will accept the results in 2024.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.032
I'm not

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.200
I don't know who that person is

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:34.667
right now,

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.203
but yes we're going to accept the results

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.771
and we're going to move forward

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.107
and work to to govern this country.

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:41.974
But I think they're going

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:42.775
to accept the results

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.609
because they're going to be

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:44.811
the president.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.713
You talked about book deals

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.047
and other reasons why

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:50.583
maybe some candidates have historically

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:51.818
wanted to get on the stage

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:52.919
rather than actually thinking that

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:53.820
they could be president.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.623
We could have a pretty big stage.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:58.725
Could be a big stage.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.993
Do you think that's good for the party

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.128
to have more voices

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.730
or will it make it harder to do

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.364
what you're saying,

00:06:04.364 --> 00:06:05.398
which is unify the party?

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:06.632
Oh, I think it speaks about the deep

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.333
bench we have

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:08.368
I mean, we have so many great

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:09.736
governors, senators,

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:11.904
congressional members, business leaders,

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:13.172
a former president.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.641
We have such a great bench of candidates.

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:16.943
I look at the Democrats,

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:17.977
what they're doing to limit

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:19.412
any competition to Biden.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.414
Look at the fact that they just changed

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:23.583
their entire primary schedule.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.952
They made sure that New Hampshire is gone

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:26.586
from being the first

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:27.787
in the nation primary. Why?

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:29.489
Because Joe Biden came in eighth.

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:31.491
So that is a president who's weak,

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:32.792
who's worried about competition

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:33.593
from his own party.

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:34.627
And we have a broad bench

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.429
ready to run for president.

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:39.098
Just one sort of philosophical question

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:40.933
that I've been wanting to ask you

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:41.701
you've seen Florida

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:42.301
Governor Ron

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.202
DeSantis

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.571
taking a really hands on approach

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:48.307
when it comes to the agenda on

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:50.343
what's going on in schools.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.043
For example,

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.211
more cultural issues,

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.213
pushing to ban funding for diversity

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:55.314
and inclusion programs

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.749
at public university,

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:59.986
expanding gender studies, trying to strip

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.387
actually stripping Disney

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:02.855
of some of its authority

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.290
for those reasons.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.626
You also see some conservatives saying

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:08.528
that's the wrong approach. That is not

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:10.530
the way the

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.532
conservative philosophy should be

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.599
because we want government

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:14.667
out of your life.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.135
What's your philosophy?

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.003
I think that's going to be up

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:17.770
to the voters

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:20.273
as as we get closer into this

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:22.341
and into this process

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:24.143
at the state level or the national level,

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.411
they take that to their voters.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:25.845
I will say

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:28.314
as a mom from the state of Michigan,

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.415
my kids wear masks.

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.716
They were out of school for two years.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.051
They're dealing with deficits.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:33.719
I've seen this in our community.

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:35.588
I wish we had a state like Florida

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:38.191
where kids my nieces were in school.

00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:40.059
They got the education they deserved.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.128
I think Republicans in general

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:44.130
are looking out for kids, things

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.031
like school choice,

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.532
making sure that kids have access

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.000
to good education.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.535
You accuse President Biden

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:51.003
of using scare tactics

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:53.539
when it comes to Republicans

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.374
wanting to cut Social Security

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.676
and Medicare.

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:59.011
Mike Pence this past week

00:07:59.212 --> 00:07:59.912
who's widely

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:01.781
expected to run for president,

00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:05.384
said that he believes that the speaker

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:06.219
he respects

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:07.353
the speaker's commitment

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:08.421
to take Social Security,

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:09.455
Medicare, off the table

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:10.623
for the debt ceiling,

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:11.824
but that in the long term

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:13.226
they should be on the table.

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:14.994
Is that the right approach?

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.295
Medicare and Social Security

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:17.163
are off the table.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.731
Speaker McCarthy said this Leader

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:19.832
McConnell has said this.

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:22.502
This is not up for negotiation.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:24.637
And I'm not going to give the Democrats

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:25.671
any leverage on this

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.006
because I get what Mike Pence is doing.

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:27.440
I think the

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:29.575
Speaker McCarthy and Leader

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:31.143
McConnell has said it's off the table.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:31.878
And to see

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:32.612
President Biden

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.813
go in front of the American people

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.081
and try and scare them

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:36.616
with something that he knew wasn't true,

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:37.884
it was a lie

00:08:37.884 --> 00:08:39.952
Republicans are going to make sure

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:41.120
that we honor our commitment

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.756
to Social Security and Medicare.

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:44.423
Before I let you go,

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:45.525
I want to ask about something

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:46.392
that's going on in your home

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:47.426
state of Michigan,

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.495
which is the person who took up

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:50.396
took your old job.

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:52.665
You were chair of the party in Michigan.

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:53.866
Christina?

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:57.169
Karamo, she is an election denier.

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.939
She on January six

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:02.742
talks about the conspiracies

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:03.309
that happened.

00:09:03.309 --> 00:09:04.877
She lost her secretary of state

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:06.812
race by double digits.

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:09.148
Does she represent your party?

00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:12.118
And will her presence

00:09:12.118 --> 00:09:13.886
as head of the party in Michigan

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:14.620
hurt your chances

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:15.788
in that very important state?

00:09:15.788 --> 00:09:17.490
You know, I don't know her very well,

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.157
and I wasn't

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:19.592
at this recent convention,

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:22.395
so the delegates chose Kristina.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:24.530
But I'm committed to Michigan.

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:25.264
It's my state.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.866
I wish you were talking about the power

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:27.300
being out.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.801
We had no power for four days.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.736
We still have 230,000 people in our state

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:31.637
with no power right now.

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:33.372
But we have a Senate seat.

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:34.674
We have House seats.

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:36.242
I love our great state.

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:37.343
And the RNC

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:38.711
is absolutely committed to Michigan.

00:09:38.711 --> 00:09:39.679
And should election

00:09:39.679 --> 00:09:41.881
denialism be a thing of the past

00:09:41.881 --> 00:09:43.983
in order to win places like Michigan,

00:09:43.983 --> 00:09:45.418
especially if there's a problem

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:46.018
with an election

00:09:46.018 --> 00:09:47.420
we should be able to talk about that.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:47.954
And I do think

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:49.422
you should be able to say, hey,

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:51.157
tabulator, we got about 20, 20.

00:09:51.157 --> 00:09:51.991
But I think we should be able

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:53.059
to talk about issues

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:53.859
that we see in elections.

00:09:53.859 --> 00:09:54.427
We should always

00:09:54.427 --> 00:09:55.428
be able to talk about that.

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:56.762
I don't think we should be able to.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:57.663
We should remove that

00:09:57.663 --> 00:09:58.531
from the conversation

00:09:58.531 --> 00:09:59.332
if people absentee

00:09:59.332 --> 00:10:00.666
ballots are not able to vote.

00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:01.133
No question.

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:02.702
But I'm talking about the entire word.

00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:04.804
I'm looking forward to 20, 24.

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:06.672
And how do we win the Senate

00:10:06.672 --> 00:10:08.574
with when we have a much better map,

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:10.042
how do we keep the House

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:11.377
and how do we win the presidency?

00:10:11.377 --> 00:10:11.978
And I will say

00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:14.113
the path forward is a united

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:14.947
Republican Party.

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.415
We've got to find our way to be there.

00:10:16.415 --> 00:10:17.717
That's what I want to be as a leader.

00:10:17.717 --> 00:10:19.251
I'm going to talk positively,

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:20.686
I'm going to be optimistic

00:10:20.686 --> 00:10:21.921
and I want to make sure

00:10:21.921 --> 00:10:22.989
that we're putting a vision forward

00:10:22.989 --> 00:10:24.924
that lets young people and women

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:26.559
and other people look at our party

00:10:26.559 --> 00:10:27.660
as something that they

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.628
aspire to be part of.

